  "details": "In the player's avatar animator, there's an \"Upright\" value that you can use to animate your crouch/prone animations, etc. \n\nHaving something similar exposed to VRCPlayerAPI (probably in the player's tracking data) would be useful for detecting when the player is crouching, prone, upright, etc. \n\nUse case would be to add \"sneak\" to your map in an interactive way where you must be physically crouched to avoid alerting a guard, etc.",
